 - **Hub workers admit only GPT-6.1 Sol** (V-1240; owner decision 2026-11-02). Canonical routing refuses every other hub model, including aliases, creative/research requests and persisted workers on send, queued delivery, resume or recovery, before provider submission. Refusal preserves model, WIP/history, pending inputs and recovery latches. Worker role defaults and tool descriptions now name hubsol; capacity messages ask to wait or report a blocker, without suggesting Claude or another fallback. Native orchestrators, manual native choices, protected local Luna, effort defaults, explicit authorized eval/API admission and existing company/privacy, ownership and quota guards retain their boundaries. No live worker/queue migration, deployment or manual restart.
 
 - **Evaluation Codex actors disable built-in apps before startup** (V-1234; `app/backend_codex.py`). Only evaluation actors receive `features.apps=false` in their private managed config, preventing default apps from registering MCP servers. Ordinary actors, base config, runtime flags and routing remain unchanged. The evaluation admission guard still rejects every residual MCP entry and nonempty pagination cursor. Source-only fix; activation requires parent acceptance, merge/push and the normal idle lifecycle before the next approved run.
